WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:05.950
In all competitive games a metagame develops, and usually with it, a mutual understanding

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:09.740
between players that not all characters are created equal.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.720
"Hakan! What the f*ck."

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:18.680
However, in today’s gaming age, developers are able to tweak metas by buffing and nerfing

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:22.740
characters through patches to make them more balanced or viable.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:25.180
And in many instances, it works.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:30.700
But occasionally it doesn’t, and some characters never truly find their place in competitive

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:31.480
play.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:37.180
In fact, some of them become targets of ridicule – they become memes.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:43.160
Meme characters are mechanically broken, community driven jokes typically selected only in poor

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:44.040
taste.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.540
But the joke is usually inconsequential, and destined to fade into obscurity.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:55.600
In Rainbow Six Siege, one such character has refused to accept this fate and ironically

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:01.040
– through his perceived uselessness – has risen as a wildly popular, cult figure within

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.200
the game’s community.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:08.040
His name is Aleksandr “Tachanka” Senaviev, and to many… he is The Lord.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:11.720
"We're not worthy! We're not worthy!"

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.280
Tachanka’s tale is a complex one.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:19.140
It’s the bittersweet story of a character who doesn’t fit into his own game and a

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.800
community that embraced him because of it.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:22.580
"I love him."

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:24.060
"Why do you love him?"

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.160
"Because of the meme."

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:31.600
It’s also the story of a passionate and dedicated development team struggling to correct

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:36.360
their greatest mistake without upsetting a fanbase who gave it a life of its own.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:41.420
But before we get into that, let’s answer the question: who is The Lord?

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:47.960
Tachanka is a release defense operator whose name references Russia’s World War 1 horse-drawn

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:53.440
machine gun carriages – which like many aspects of Russian life had their own song:

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:10.480
While Tachanka might be heavily armored, he lacks the mobility of his 20th century namesake,

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:13.080
and is one of the slowest operators in Siege.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:20.340
And although his primary and secondary weapons are actually half decent – the main source

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.880
for his ridicule lies in his special ability.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:25.540
"LMG mounted! And loaded!"

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:32.900
That’s right, Tachanka can set-up a mounted, drum-fed LMG, capable of tearing through drywall

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.060
just as easily as his opponents.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:40.200
Now, in theory, this might sound pretty f*cking badass.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:51.720
But in practice… not so much.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:59.760
"Right I'm saving that, there's something wrong with this Chanka gun. There's something wrong with it."

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:04.400
The problem is that Rainbow Six Siege is about movement and information.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:09.580
And because almost all surfaces can be destroyed or penetrated by gunfire, standing still in

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.820
the open is a recipe for being made into swiss cheese.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:21.340
Unfortunately for Tachanka, his turret simply doesn’t have a great place in the game.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:26.500
It takes forever to set-up and take down, your movement is limited while using it, and

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:31.300
you can’t set it up too close to cover because the weapon needs room to be maneuvered.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:38.260
In fact, Tachanka’s overall kit is ranked so lowly by players that many even think Recruit

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:43.860
– the default operator selected if you fail
to pick another – is considered a more viable

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:46.780
pick because he offers more in game utility.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:52.700
All of these factors combine to make Tachanka one of the least picked and effective operators

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:53.540
in Siege.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:59.840
And only a few months after the game’s release, he had become known as one of its worst operators.

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:31.420
But Ubisoft's “mistake” had developed an underdog status and over time a strange fame.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:35.780
Tachanka had ascended from being a mere mortal to Lord Tachanka.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:41.680
Seemingly, the first time someone called him Lord Tachanka was YouTuber MicrowaveGaming.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:45.940
"I'm also looking for more clips for a kill of the week montage by you the viewers.

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:51.060
If you would like to participate, then drop me a link or send me a video. If you have an ace with Tachanka

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:55.100
then chances are you're gonna be number one because ALL HAIL LORD CHANKA!"

00:04:55.160 --> 00:05:01.440
And the basis of the Lord Tachanka meme is that he is so bad, he's actually incredible.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:05.880
People love him in the same way that they love watching The Room... “you’re tearing

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:10.240
me apart Lisa!” ...4th of July hot-dog eating
contests...

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:15.080
"You're witnessing greatness athletic mastery. This is not a parlor trick, this is not slight of hand,

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.720
This is Major League Eating's best ever..."

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:17.960
and Star Wars?

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:20.820
“IT’S A TRAP” Wait a second, did
you add this?

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:22.900
I would never agree to this…

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:30.620
Anyway, in an attempt to make Tachanka more balanced, Ubisoft introduced changes later

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:35.220
in the year, during the mid-season reinforcements for Operation Red Crow.

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:40.000
The adjustments included a bulletproof shield for his turret and some additional recoil

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.000
to the gun itself.

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:44.080
And it was in that update that Ubisoft began

00:05:44.082 --> 00:05:46.860
leaning into the community’s love for the

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:51.300
Lord Tachanka meme – highlighted by the inscription of the Russian word for “Lord”

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:56.760
on his new turret shield and a special appearance by his voice actor Anatoly Zinoviev on the

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:57.780
reveal stream.

00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:00.960
"If you want to say what's up to the chat too, they're here."

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:01.700
"Sup guys!"

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:04.560
"They're really excited to see you here."

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:06.600
“LMG MOUNTED AND LOADED!”

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:09.640
"That's really awesome."

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:15.040
Yes, your eyes do not deceive you – the Lord even has a fan-created emote which you

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:17.040
will see spammed in Twitch chat.

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:23.740
In the end the changes brought by Operation Red Crow did little to make Tachanka more

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:27.940
effective, and even today, his pick-rate remains quite low.

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:33.600
But in spite of this, his meme god status has continued to be supported by Ubisoft,

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:37.900
who in May of this year released an actual Lord Tachanka bundle.

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:44.260
And at the Six Major in Paris, Siege’s esports director Alexandre Remy, explained to us why

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:46.660
Ubisoft chose to embrace The Lord meme.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:31.580
While most interaction with the Tachanka meme happens outside of the game, the Lord does

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:34.440
make the occasional ranked appearance.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:37.400
Just.... with questionable motivations.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:42.340
“It’s only for when you’re beating someone like 3-0 and you want to rub it in that you’re

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:46.180
better than them. That's all, that's all he is.” “You’ve gotta spawn peek on the turret.

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:47.250
It’s an embarrassment isn’t it?

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:50.300
If you get peeked with that turret and you die in spawn, that’s bad.”

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:53.260
“You know when you’re playing a game as well and someone uses it, you don’t get angry.

00:07:53.260 --> 00:07:56.900
You just sort of laugh and go along with it and it’s absolutely fantastic.

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:58.440
It’s a great thing, to be honest.”

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:04.000
Even though Tachanka is often used for in-game trolling, his current state as a broken but

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:08.220
beloved operator presents a complicated issue for Ubisoft.

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:41.200
And therein lies the problem.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:46.240
How do you change the character without completely destroying his community-created identity?

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:52.280
We asked Siege fans and personalities how they’d react to a significant Tachanka rework

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:54.980
and their answers only highlighted the division.

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:59.030
“I’d probably be very unhappy, because you just can't change a meme like that.

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:03.340
Like if they tried to make him more competitively viable, it would remove the meme completely.

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:04.500
I'd probably be unhappy yeah."

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:06.300
"I think it's good for the community, to have something.

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:11.080
It's on a lot of t-shirts, it's the banter
of the community, I don't think they

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:11.740
should touch him."

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:12.540
“I’d love it.

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:14.340
He needs a complete rework.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:20.100
As soon as they gave other operators moveable LMGs he became irrelevant.”

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:25.720
"I have no idea what that change would be, a plausible change would be that his turret can shoot through

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:30.360
sheilds and that would actually be like legitimate, so then you would have a direct deterrent

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:34.100
against a shield pushing site because you have a turret that can shoot through that kinda stuff.

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:35.700
So that would be really cool."

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:39.140
So the question then becomes: What's more important?

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:45.500
Having another viable operator in your game’s meta or leaving a community-born meme undisturbed?

00:09:45.500 --> 00:09:48.320
It’s a puzzle that Ubisoft is still trying to solve.

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:02.780
Regardless of where you stand on Lord Tachanka – whether you think he is a dying meme,

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:05.080
or he's Siege’s patron saint.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:09.880
Whether you think he should be buffed or just left alone – he elicits a reaction.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:14.160
And his presence in the game has not only contributed to the formation of Siege’s

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:19.540
unique communal identity, but it has also further informed Ubisoft’s design choices

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:21.400
behind operators going forward.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:50.440
So there you have it – Lord Tachanka.

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:55.600
Proof that a meme is capable of positively shaping both a community’s identity and

00:10:55.600 --> 00:11:00.560
the development philosophy behind one of esports’ most exciting, rising games.

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:04.360
Sounds like more of a miracle than a mistake, right?

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:10.140
You know man, I always think that we're doing the Lord’s work with this show.

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:14.840
Hey man, The Lord loves all equally.

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:16.560
Who told you that?

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:17.560
He did.

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:21.680
“Tachanka will always stand by you”.

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:26.160
"How do you feel when people pick him instead of you?

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:32.200
"I mean there are people doing a lot of mistakes, a lot of stupid things.

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:41.100
I don't know what to say about these kind of people choosing Tachanka instead of Blackbeard I mean

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.780
it's a sort of insane."

00:11:45.320 --> 00:11:50.300
"What would you say to all of those people who are proclaiming the lordship of Tachanka."

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:55.900
"You guys are wrong and I will come for you."

